# Vite emits content-hashed filenames under /assets, so they can never go
# stale: cache them for a year and never ask again.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The built-in fonts (2 MB of Inter and Noto) keep their names, since the
# font library knows them by their paths: a week without asking, then
# revalidated in the background, so a visit never waits on them and a
# changed font still arrives within days.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=2592000

# The page itself needs no rule. It is the one unhashed file, and Pages
# already serves it at / with max-age=0, must-revalidate. A rule for
# /index.html would never match, because Pages redirects that path to /.

# The last two are cross-origin isolation, which is what lets the page and
# the engine worker share memory: the tile slabs, and the ring the pen's
# samples travel through (ARCHITECTURE.md, "The threads"). The dev server
# sets the same pair in vite.config.ts. require-corp also blocks any
# cross-origin subresource that does not opt in through CORP or CORS; the
# app loads none.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
